<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Transitional//EN" "http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-transitional.dtd">
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" lang="en">
<head>
<meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=UTF-8" />
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
<meta name="x-apple-disable-message-reformatting" />
<meta name="color-scheme" content="light" />
<meta name="supported-color-schemes" content="light" />
<title>{{ site.wordmark }} — the {{ site.publishDay }} essay</title>

<!--
  =========================================================
  ON PURPOSE — EMAIL TEMPLATE
  The Sunday essay by Tim

  THIS FILE IS GENERATED. Do not edit the output — edit the
  essay in content/essays/ and run `npm run email -- NNN`
  again. The templates live in src/_includes/email/.

  STRUCTURE (top to bottom)
    1. Masthead        lowercase, centred
    2. Title           big, centred
    3. Hook            centred subtitle — the one-liner from the site
    4. Utility line    READ ON MY WEBSITE · N MIN READ
    5. Sponsor slot    commented out. Uncomment when you have one.
    6. The essay       left aligned, short paragraphs
    7. Sign-off
    8. Subscribe panel for forwarded readers
    9. Footer + unsubscribe

  EACH WEEK you change: preview text, title, hook, read time,
  and the essay. All of it comes from the markdown file.

  WHY THE CODE LOOKS LIKE 2004
  Tables and inline styles. Outlook renders email with Microsoft
  Word's engine and ignores most modern CSS. This is deliberate —
  don't let anyone "tidy it up" into divs and classes.

  ---------------------------------------------------------
  V2 — after testing on iOS Gmail, iOS Outlook and iPad Gmail
  ---------------------------------------------------------
  Buttondown's free plan strips the <head>, so the <style> block
  and the colour-scheme meta tags below never reach the inbox.
  Every client tested therefore force-inverted the email. The
  layout held. Two dark panels did not.

  THE RULE THAT CAME OUT OF IT:
  encode meaning with HUE and RULES, never with light-vs-dark.
  Inversion remaps lightness and mostly leaves hue alone. Brass
  (#C08A3E) survives everywhere, and so do hairline borders. Ink
  (#26241F) and paper (#F1EFEA) sit at opposite extremes and both
  collapse toward the same mid grey — so anything relying on the
  contrast between those two disappears.

  Changed in v2:
   1. Active 2x2 cell   dark fill -> brass fill
   2. Subscribe panel   added a 2px brass border
   3. Outer background  kept, with the trade-off documented inline

  Not fixable on the free plan, and not worth paying to fix:
   - iOS linkifies dates ("Thursday afternoon" went blue). The
     rule that suppresses it lives in the stripped <style> block.
   - Link colour is Buttondown's, set globally by the tint colour
     under Settings > General > Branding. Currently #26241F, which
     is what makes the brass button read correctly.
   - The <style> block is kept regardless: it costs nothing, and it
     works if you ever move to Naked mode or another provider.
  =========================================================
-->

<!-- Web fonts: Apple Mail and a few others will use these; everything
     else quietly falls back to Georgia, which is close enough that most
     readers won't notice. Never rely on the web font for legibility. -->
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Newsreader:ital,opsz,wght@0,6..72,300..600;1,6..72,300..500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />

<style type="text/css">
  body { margin:0 !important; padding:0 !important; width:100% !important; background-color:#F1EFEA; }
  table { border-collapse:collapse !important; }
  img { border:0; outline:none; text-decoration:none; -ms-interpolation-mode:bicubic; }

  .ExternalClass { width:100%; }
  .ExternalClass, .ExternalClass p, .ExternalClass td { line-height:100%; }

  a[x-apple-data-detectors] {
    color:inherit !important; text-decoration:none !important;
    font-size:inherit !important; font-family:inherit !important; font-weight:inherit !important;
  }

  @media screen and (max-width:640px) {
    .container { width:100% !important; }
    .pad       { padding-left:24px !important; padding-right:24px !important; }
    .title     { font-size:30px !important; line-height:1.15 !important; }
    .hook      { font-size:18px !important; }
    .quote     { font-size:20px !important; }
    .body-copy { font-size:17px !important; }
    .cell-2x2  { font-size:13px !important; padding:14px 12px !important; }
  }
</style>
</head>

<body style="margin:0; padding:0; background-color:#F1EFEA;">

<!-- PREVIEW TEXT — the grey line beside your subject in the inbox.
     It comes from `previewText` in the essay's front matter. It does more
     for opens than anything else here, so it's authored, never generated.
     The invisible characters after it stop Gmail pulling in body text. -->
<div style="display:none; font-size:1px; color:#F1EFEA; line-height:1px; max-height:0; max-width:0; opacity:0; overflow:hidden;">
  {{ essay.previewText }}
  &nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;
</div>

<!-- THE SEAM, and the one judgement call in this file.
     In dark mode this background and Buttondown's own wrapper invert to slightly
     different darks, so a faint step shows at the top edge of the email. Deleting
     background-color below closes the seam — but it also gives up the warm paper
     colour in LIGHT mode, where Buttondown's wrapper is plain white. That's a bad
     trade: the paper is a signature, the seam is a hairline. Left in deliberately.
     If you decide the seam bothers you more than the white does, delete the
     background-color declaration here and on <body> above, and re-test both modes. -->
<table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="background-color:#F1EFEA;">
<tr><td align="center" style="padding:0;">

  <!-- Content sits directly on the background. No card, no border. -->
  <table role="presentation" class="container" width="640" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="width:640px; max-width:640px;">

    <!-- ============ 1. MASTHEAD ============ -->
    <tr><td class="pad" align="center" style="padding:52px 60px 0 60px;">
      <div style="font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif; font-size:21px; color:#3F6E8C; line-height:1.3;">
        {{ site.wordmark | lower }} &nbsp;·&nbsp; the {{ site.publishDay | lower }} essay by {{ site.author | lower }}
      </div>
    </td></tr>

    <!-- ============ 2. TITLE ============ -->
    <tr><td class="pad" align="center" style="padding:38px 60px 0 60px;">
      <h1 class="title" style="margin:0; font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;
                 font-weight:normal; font-size:42px; line-height:1.1; color:#26241F;">
        {{ essay.title }}
      </h1>
    </td></tr>

    <!-- ============ 3. HOOK ============ -->
    <tr><td class="pad" align="center" style="padding:22px 70px 0 70px;">
      <div class="hook" style="font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;
                  font-size:21px; line-height:1.45; color:#6B665D;">
        {{ essay.emailHook }}
      </div>
    </td></tr>

    <!-- ============ 4. UTILITY LINE ============ -->
    <tr><td class="pad" align="center" style="padding:26px 60px 0 60px;
             font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:11px; letter-spacing:2px;
             text-transform:uppercase; color:#6B665D;">
      <a href="{{ essayUrl }}"
         style="color:#6B665D; text-decoration:underline;">Read on my website</a>
      &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; {{ essay.readTime }} min read
    </td></tr>

    <!-- ============ 5. SPONSOR SLOT ============
         Left in, commented out. When you're big enough to sell one,
         delete the comment markers and fill it in. Duplicate for a second.

    <tr><td class="pad" style="padding:38px 60px 0 60px;">
      <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="background-color:#E7E3DB;">
        <tr><td style="padding:26px 28px;">
          <div style="font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:10px; letter-spacing:2px;
                      text-transform:uppercase; color:#6B665D; padding-bottom:12px;">Sponsored &middot; Company name</div>
          <div style="font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,serif; font-size:20px; font-weight:600; color:#26241F; padding-bottom:10px;">
            The offer headline
          </div>
          <div style="font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; color:#4A453C; padding-bottom:20px;">
            Two sentences on what it is and why this audience would care.
          </div>
          <table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
            <tr><td style="background-color:#26241F;">
              <a href="#" style="display:inline-block; padding:12px 22px; font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;
                 font-size:13px; font-weight:bold; color:#FAF8F4; text-decoration:none;">Call to action &rarr;</a>
            </td></tr>
          </table>
        </td></tr>
      </table>
    </td></tr>

    ============ END SPONSOR SLOT ============ -->

    <!-- Divider before the essay -->
    <tr><td class="pad" style="padding:44px 60px 0 60px;">
      <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
        <tr><td style="border-top:1px solid #DDD8CF; font-size:0; line-height:0;">&nbsp;</td></tr>
      </table>
    </td></tr>
